1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:01,636
This is Repeat AI.

2
00:00:01,636 --> 00:00:03,536
Here's how it fits into your day.

3
00:00:05,550 --> 00:00:07,158
It starts with your spreadsheet.

4
00:00:07,158 --> 00:00:11,017
You can bring in a Google Sheet link or an Excel file.

5
00:00:11,017 --> 00:00:12,624
We'll use the link here.

6
00:00:12,624 --> 00:00:17,769
Choose the buildings you work with, and Repeat AI brings in your leads, organised by building.

7
00:00:17,769 --> 00:00:21,306
From there, they're ready to work with on the Sellers page.

8
00:00:25,550 --> 00:00:31,532
This is where you can see everyone in one place: their details, their building, and where things stand.

9
00:00:31,532 --> 00:00:34,523
Filter by prospects, appraisals, for sale, or not interested.

10
00:00:34,523 --> 00:00:37,514
Sold today flags a fresh transaction in that building.

11
00:00:37,514 --> 00:00:42,831
Open a seller and you can see what sold, when it sold, and for how much.

12
00:00:42,831 --> 00:00:49,145
With WhatsApp connected, those transactions can feed into automated follow-ups, giving you something useful to share with your sellers.

13
00:00:52,550 --> 00:00:56,801
You can use the default message, or make it sound more like you.

14
00:00:56,801 --> 00:01:03,013
In Message templates, write your own wording and drop in the seller's name, their building, and the latest transactions.

15
00:01:03,013 --> 00:01:10,861
The preview fills those details in as you go, so you can see exactly what the message will look like before you save it.

16
00:01:14,550 --> 00:01:16,932
You also decide when those follow-ups go out.

17
00:01:16,932 --> 00:01:22,588
Schedule lets you spread your buildings across the week, so you can organise them around the way you work.

18
00:01:22,588 --> 00:01:24,970
Here, we've added buildings from Monday through Thursday.

19
00:01:24,970 --> 00:01:29,137
Save the plan, and the weekly schedule controls which buildings get follow-ups each day.

20
00:01:29,137 --> 00:01:30,626
Days left empty stay off.

21
00:01:35,550 --> 00:01:40,815
Over in Listings, you can track the buildings you cover and spot apartments that have dropped in price.

22
00:01:40,815 --> 00:01:44,032
Open a building, then an apartment, to get a closer look.

23
00:01:44,032 --> 00:01:49,004
You can follow the asking price on the chart, and check Activity to see when it changed.

24
00:01:49,004 --> 00:01:51,929
It's a useful bit of context before your next conversation.

25
00:01:57,550 --> 00:02:02,013
And you can connect the tools you already use, from spreadsheets to email and calendars.

26
00:02:04,350 --> 00:02:08,732
For a quicker way to get things done, there's Ask Repeat in the corner.

27
00:02:08,732 --> 00:02:11,862
Type what you need, or talk to it using voice.

28
00:02:11,862 --> 00:02:16,556
It can find sellers, summarise market activity, and help with things like templates and scheduling.

29
00:02:16,556 --> 00:02:18,747
Here, it's prepared a new message template.

30
00:02:18,747 --> 00:02:23,129
You can read it through and confirm the change when you're happy with it.

31
00:02:27,550 --> 00:02:31,991
Repeat AI is available on the web, Windows and mobile, so you can pick up where you left off.
